body:
@yogeshktm, thanks for wanting to tackle this issue. Modifying the white space is not the direction we're looking for for this fix. We're looking for the same behaviour for a code snippet in the body of a post, i.e. scrolling.

https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/833231/103707728-309c7b80-4f7d-11eb-8375-4c45fefe4fe6.mp4

Having said that, I still think this would be a great first issue for you. Let us know if you'd still like to work on it with the proposed fix.

Team, @nickytonline 

i have found `overflow-x:auto` is missing in the parent elements would have cause this issue. as far as my investigation we need below code changes to fix this issue. 

```
.comment-form.preview-open,.comments-container,.comment-form__inner{
   overflow-x:auto;
}
```

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/3961774/103795848-800da500-506c-11eb-9c83-556540a12033.png)

i tried finding scss related to these changes in the repository but i can't able to find scss files related to these. i am very new here. can anyone help me on guiding me to find the scss or is there any other way to add styles here ?

Thanks in advance.
